# 3. ADVANCED PRINT() METHODS & OUTPUTS
# ==========================================

# A) Using the `end` Parameter
# - By default, print() automatically jumps to a new line at the end.
# - You can change this behavior using `end=" "`. This prints things on the SAME line.
print("Hello", end=" ")
print("World!")  # Output: Hello World!

# B) Numbers vs Text in Print
# - Unlike text/strings, we do NOT enclose numbers or mathematical operations in quotation marks.
print(3)
print(300)
print(5 * 2)  # Performs multiplication directly inside print (Output: 10)
print(7 + 3)  # Performs addition directly inside print (Output: 10)
